- 2026-08-21: New tooling per direction: (1) tools/detect_negation_contrast.py v2 — sentence-level Not-X-But-Y detector with STRONG/MEDIUM/WEAK tiers; evaluation mode only, not wired into checker. First run: 3 STRONG (both user-flagged ch11 lines caught), 4 MEDIUM, 38 WEAK — WEAK tier reveals negate-then-act is the book's pervasive choice-rendering move, so adoption decision pending. Known edge case: attribution fragments after dialogue can mis-split. (2) tools/extract_dialogue.py -> tests/DIALOGUE.md (190 lines). (3) Motif co-occurrence matrix in analyzer — found coin+warm 75% FUSED, wall+hum 73% FUSED (two labels, one image). (4) tools/cut_candidates.py safety ranking + compression lens (fixed regex bug: 'chapter_01' vs ch\\d+). (5) Modern calibration point added: Little Brother excerpt (CC, 2008) — ours runs half its dialogue share and double its fear/grief rates.
- 2026-08-24: Negation-contrast adopted into checker: NC-01 (STRONG/MEDIUM frames) warns; NC-02 caps WEAK frames at 5% of chapter sentences, floor 3. Logic shared via tools/patterns_negation.py so standalone evaluator and checker cannot drift. Current run: 8 warnings, 0 errors. P9 AI-Pattern Hunter persona added to red team with quantification mandate; its scan found one new signature — abstract "the X of" frames at 15.7/10k (canon ~2-4) — now tracked in the analyzer's AI-signature panel (triads, not-just, participial openers all at floor). Fresh dated artifacts created: docs/story_assessment_2026-08-24.md (raw 7.32 / adjusted 7.06, unchanged scores — tooling-only delta) and tests/redteam/REDTEAM_REPORT_2026-08-24.md (round 5, nine personas). Pipeline updated: dated-artifact convention + panel roster + negation governance.
