- 2026-08-25: Texture-starvation countermeasure adopted (user question + external review motif-capture warning): PP ledger now supports status:texture - deliberately unconnected details are PROTECTED LOCALS, exempt from orphan warnings, reviewed at zero-based audits. Three existing textures registered (water-seller, excavation vendor, harbor vowels). Pipeline observation register extended: every chapter should contain at least one detail that pays off nowhere. Rationale: all framework metrics reward connection; without explicit protection, integration pressure will eventually sand away unexplained life.
- 2026-08-25: C6 Texture Lover added to Council of Readers - audience member who rewards well-written unconnected detail and distrusts over-integration; special duty: co-curates the TX texture register each session (alive vs inserted-trivia rulings) and flags all-machinery chapters. First session: 8.5; inventory verdict - water-seller/radio/harbor-vowels/kettle ruled alive and protected; ch6-ch7 chambers flagged as residue-thin (all function, no ordinary life); burst aftermath could hold one more useless detail. Council mean now 8.1 across six members.

- 2026-08-25: C6 redefined from "Texture Lover" to "Mood Reader" per user direction - loves mood/vibes/atmosphere FIRST; unconnected texture is loved as a consequence, not hunted as a goal. New instrument: Atmosphere panel in analyzer (per-chapter smell/light/weather/temperature/sound lexicon counts, airless-flagging). First reading caught ch10 (ribbon chapter) as sensorily airless -> one in-mood anchor added (rain against the window during playback). Also fixed real analyzer bug discovered en route: dialogue-share was computed over the JOINED corpus, letting a single quote imbalance bleed matches across chapter boundaries (inflated corpus to 33%); now computed per-file and summed (true value 16%). C6 score 8.5 stands under redefined scope.

